{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1558768-shperes-over-paradigm-or-not","id":1558768,"title":"Shperes over Paradigm, or...not?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-03-10T04:15:55-07:00","id":1558768,"title":"Shperes over Paradigm, or...not?","content":"Hi everyone.<br /> I've been running games of Mages since the revised, and I've been running M20 since it came out.<br /> Yesterday I was having a conversation with a fellow player and a doubtr struck me. I'm sure this topic has been extensively discussed, but I couldn't find an answer, so here I am, sharing the same doubt, looking for wisdom.<br /> English is not my first language, I hope I'll be able to properly explain what my question is. Here we go:<br /> <br /> Now, I've always interpreted spheres as something separate from the character paradigm, as in &quot;Yoiur character may believe that she can make object flying with her mind, but on your character sheet you need dots in forces to do that.&quot; (this is an example to simplify the concept).<br /> <br /> But what happens when this distinction between the mechanical aspect of the sphere and the paradigm of the character becomes manifest in game?<br /> <br /> Let's take the example above and expand it a bit.<br /> <br /> Terry's paradigm is all about psychic powers. Everything he does (according to Terry's belief) comes from his enhanced mental prowess.<br /> Now Terry is waiting in his room, his eyes closed, sitting in the lotus position, hoovering a few inches from the ground.<br /> <br /> Mechanically he'd be using force, to levitate.<br /> But Terry is sure, it's his mind power that lets him do that.<br /> <br /> Enters Terry's best friend, Anne.<br /> Anne, looks at his friend and scan for any psychic energy in the room.<br /> None.<br /> In fact, unless Anne extend her perception to the pertinence of force, she wouldn't see nothing at all.<br /> <br /> Terry comes out of his meditation, and Anne confronts him.<br /> &quot;Dude, I thought you were a psychic! &quot;<br /> &quot;I am!&quot;<br /> &quot;Well, whatever you were doing right now, has nothing to do with your mind! I'd seen it!&quot;<br /> <br /> Forgive me the sillyness of the example but it's to better explain what I'm getting at.<br /> <br /> Now what could potentially happen? Terry's paradigm tells him that his mind lets him levitate, and for all it's worth the whole concept of the character is build around this premise. But now the mechanics are telling not only the player (who of course, knows the distinction between spheres and paradigm), but the character that in game, his paradigm is not &quot;correct&quot;, I guess?<br /> <br /> This kind of situation could potentially lead to interesting scenes and exploration of paradigm from a game standpoint, and I'm all up for it. But how the mechanics of the needed sphere for an effect impact the &quot;fiction&quot; (for lack of a better term) of the story?<br /> <br /> Am I twisting this thing, or there's something I'm missing?<br /> <br /> I love this game, it's probably my favourite, and doubts like this, in my opinion are what makes it even more engaging. I'd love to hear some advice from you people, this community is amazing!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28492-sistofelis","user":"Sistofelis","date":". 03-10-2026, 07:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28492-sistofelis","name":"Sistofelis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-12T03:06:55-07:00","id":1558817,"title":"","content":"Terry's understanding of the Spheres, if he has one, would be that they are fundamentally commanded by the mind.<br /> <br /> &quot;Sensing psychic energy? Well there was enough force to keep me hovering a few inches off the ground, and that energy comes from me concentrating, so definitionally I'd call that a form of 'psychic energy'.&quot;<br /> <br /> Essentially, to Terry, Forces comes from mental energy, whatever other Mages might say. And to be fair to him, if you were to turn off his brain, he wouldn't be able to use Forces! The mind does seem to be crucial.<br /> <br /> The trickier example is Mages who believe all their powers come from spirits or aliens or other unearthly forces. How does that Mage explain it when their powers work, only to then be told that they are 100% cut off from the Umbra and there's no way any spirit could have manifested the effect? Presumably they'd just cope and say that these forces can pierce reality via their Avatar, but still, it's interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-12T06:48:16-07:00","id":1558820,"title":"","content":"Agreed, psychic powers it's not a great example because &quot;Warping reality with your mind&quot; and &quot;Warping reality with your Will&quot; are very similar concepts :P . It <i>could</i> be a problem if there's a power that blocks or detects psychic numina but wouldn't work on Magic(k) - but then one could question the reliability of said power. But, yeah, this is an issue for many Paradigms.<br /> <br /> Spirits that should be present, but you can clearly see they aren't (with Spirit 2) it's the classic example. Another example could be &quot;what happens if you sabbotage the machinery a Technocrat it's using as an Instrument - does still function if the Technocrat doesn't know it shouldn't?&quot;<br /> <br /> There's two ways AFAIK to rule this, that are both supported in the books to at least some extent.<br /> <br /> *One school of tought it's that magick will work as long as the mage believes it does. This can lead to situations where belief it's challenged (the Technocrat it's giving maintenance to his gizmo, and discovers the sabbotage, yet it worked a second ago)<br /> <br /> *Another it's that Paradigm works at a &quot;meta level&quot; and thus if it's &quot;technology&quot; and there's a reason &quot;technology&quot; shouldn't work, then it won't work (wheter the mage knows about it or not). This can be confusing and a bit difficult to adjudicate (when the books try, it often looks like a punishment: Like with the Spirit prerequisite for Shamanic practices on HDYDT), but I think it's the most thematic if it can be done well.<br /> <br /> The first option it's the canon answer of 1rst edition. Back then all mages knew on a level they were reality warping with their willpower, but needed instruments because of inexperience. Latter on Mages started to actually <i>believe </i>ontheir Paradigm, and thus the 2nd option surges as an interesting posibility, but the 1rst one was never really abandoned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-12T10:34:19-07:00","id":1558824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>twig</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1558768-shperes-over-paradigm-or-not?p=1558817#post1558817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Essentially, to Terry, Forces comes from mental energy, whatever other Mages might say. And to be fair to him, if you were to turn off his brain, he wouldn't be able to use Forces! The mind does seem to be crucial.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a great point to help me further explain my doubt!<br /> <br /> Suppose Terry's brain has been shut down.<br /> <br /> IF we take away the possibility for him to use Force (since according to his paradigm, those comes from his Mind), then we're putting &quot;Paradigm&quot; over &quot;Spheres&quot; in terms of what is predominant in influencing the fiction (where &quot;Fiction&quot; as I intended is the &quot;narrative reality of the game&quot;).<br /> And that could be absolutely fine, but that would mean that Terry's paradigm would put Mind as a pre requisite to use the other spheres. Wich I'll admit can be intriguing from a rp stand point, but it's not (as far as I know) a rule.<br /> <br /> IF we would allow Terry to access forces even when his Mind is turned off, then we would be leaning more towards a Sphere (as in &quot;the dots the character has on his sheets) over Paradigm, in terms of what influence more, again, the fiction.<br /> <br /> That's the core of my doubt, thanks for providing me a hook to elaborate (I hope) better.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>twig</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1558768-shperes-over-paradigm-or-not?p=1558817#post1558817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The trickier example is Mages who believe all their powers come from spirits or aliens or other unearthly forces. How does that Mage explain it when their powers work, only to then be told that they are 100% cut off from the Umbra and there's no way any spirit could have manifested the effect? Presumably they'd just cope and say that these forces can pierce reality via their Avatar, but still, it's interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I completely agree.<br /> To be honest the actual situation me and my froiends were discussing about were the example of a mage (a spiritis tuned with the elemental spirit of a volcano) casting a Fireball (I know, very petty, but again, for example sake). He would be using Force, but according to his Paradigm, the Spirit from the Volcano are granting him that power.<br /> <br /> If Anne (who is clearly Hellbent on disruptin his frined's belief at this point) would cast a detect spirit spell, she would find no spiritual energy.<br /> <br /> I proposed at first a solution similar to the one you suggested. Maybe the Spirit of the Volcano are actually granting the guy their powers despite him being lacking in the spiritual affinity, because they were moved by his devotion.<br /> <br /> But still, my doubt remains.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28492-sistofelis","name":"Sistofelis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-12T10:43:45-07:00","id":1558825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1558768-shperes-over-paradigm-or-not?p=1558820#post1558820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreed, psychic powers it's not a great example because &quot;Warping reality with your mind&quot; and &quot;Warping reality with your Will&quot; are very similar concepts :P . It <i>could</i> be a problem if there's a power that blocks or detects psychic numina but wouldn't work on Magic(k) - but then one could question the reliability of said power. But, yeah, this is an issue for many Paradigms.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see what you're saying, maybe mind wasn't a great example, but the issue is not what &quot;Terry&quot; believes, it's more &quot;If a Paradigm does not comprehend in the belief system it summarize every orher sphere, what happens when they comes into play?&quot;<br /> Since, sure Terry might believe (as he absolutely should) that all he does comes from his mind, but when &quot;rule-wise&quot; he's put in front of the fact that it's not how Magick works, then what happens?<br /> <br /> I completely agree with you, it's an issue for many paradigms.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1558768-shperes-over-paradigm-or-not?p=1558820#post1558820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Another it's that Paradigm works at a &quot;meta level&quot; and thus if it's &quot;technology&quot; and there's a reason &quot;technology&quot; shouldn't work, then it won't work (wheter the mage knows about it or not). This can be confusing and a bit difficult to adjudicate (when the books try, it often looks like a punishment: Like with the Spirit prerequisite for Shamanic practices on HDYDT), but I think it's the most thematic if it can be done well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree it's usually what I tend to consider as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1558768-shperes-over-paradigm-or-not?p=1558820#post1558820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first option it's the canon answer of 1rst edition. Back then all mages knew on a level they were reality warping with their willpower, but needed instruments because of inexperience. Latter on Mages started to actually <i>believe </i>ontheir Paradigm, and thus the 2nd option surges as an interesting posibility, but the 1rst one was never really abandoned.</div> </div> </div> </div>[/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> Yeah, I talked with some other players who were coming from older edition, and the issue of Paradigm was exactly how you're describing.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28492-sistofelis","name":"Sistofelis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-13T05:07:16-07:00","id":1558831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sistofelis</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see what you're saying, maybe mind wasn't a great example, but the issue is not what &quot;Terry&quot; believes, it's more &quot;If a Paradigm does not comprehend in the belief system it summarize every orher sphere, what happens when they comes into play?&quot;<br /> Since, sure Terry might believe (as he absolutely should) that all he does comes from his mind, but when &quot;rule-wise&quot; he's put in front of the fact that it's not how Magick works, then what happens?</div> </div> </div> </div>I see, you're wondering about cases where the Paradigm posits as the &quot;cause&quot; of the effect an element that belongs under the conceptual umbrella of another Sphere that wasn't involved on the effect. So what now?<br /> <br /> Core RAW, no: What matters for the mechanics are the mechanics of the Effect, not the mechanics thta could be alluded by Paradigm. So, levitating it's Forces regardless of your belief. <hr /><br /> HDYDT has a (very unpopular) optional rule where, yes, you should have the Sphere of the concept as prerequisite. Shamans need to have Spirit 2 and include it on every Effect. In the case of psychic powers, Mind 2, or maybe even 3, would be a prerequisite to cast your levitation effect. Ppl call this &quot;Sphere Tax&quot;<br /> <br /> There's something to be said in favor of HDYDT &quot;Sphere Tax&quot;, tho - it often isn't as onerous as it looks like because Paradigms that are deeply invested on the phenomena of some Sphere are most likely going to gravitate to that Sphere anyways (so it's a &quot;tax&quot; that you were going to pay anyway). And, mechanically, it adds the flavorful <i>dis</i>advantage that your spells associated with that Sphere can be sensed and/or countered by using the additional Sphere. I.E: If you use &quot;fire spirits&quot; for Forces, and thus have to add Spirit 2 to the mix, then you can counter the spell with Spirit.<br /> <br /> The problem with that optional rule it's that it's all disadvantages, it's flavorful but it sort of fells like a punishment - even if not a very severe one. <hr /><br /> Personally I preffer to detach Spheres and Paradigms at the level of mechanics, and if anything rejoin them on the level of the narrative afterwards. To me, Forces when used by a psychic <i>it's</i> psychic. It doesn't <i>need</i> Mind to be psychic. It needs Mind if he wants to add stuff like telepathy to his arsenal of psychic powers.<br /> <br /> And (here's where we go to houserule territory) his use of Forces it's going to &quot;sense&quot; as psychic to relevant powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-13-2026, 08:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-13T07:35:46-07:00","id":1558834,"title":"","content":"This is going to get long, so I\u2019ll summarize first. Spheres, both mechanically and narratively, cover influence and power over a domain, they don\u2019t cover the paradigmatic elements used to cast. Things get muddy quickly if we try to make them do so.<br /> <br /> Spheres exist both in character and out of character so I\u2019ll tackle them both ways.<br /> <br /> Out of character they are supposed to be a rules system for handling just about any kind of magic system. There are limitations to that, but in general the same effect should have the same sphere requirement regardless of paradigm. Your psychic does not need Mind to levitate. He needs Forces 2. Or possibly Forces 2/Life 2 if he\u2019s going to move outside of the range of the original casting and needs to lock the spell to himself.<br /> <br /> In character, the spheres are a system mages cobbled together to talk about capabilities across different paradigms. Most mages treat them as a social construct, not a statement of metaphysical fact. Indeed, one of the purposes of spheres is that it doesn\u2019t matter if the Hermetic is using the interactions of the great Crystal Spheres to levitate, while the Akashic is supporting himself with projected chi, and the Virtual Adept is mathematically calculating the proper movements to counterbalance gravity, they can still talk about the effects using the same spheres.<br /> <br /> In neither case do the Spheres cover anything to do with how a mage paradigmatically gets to the effect, and usually this is really clear. However, whenever a paradigm starts to sound a lot like a specific sphere (commonly Mind, Spirit, and Prime) it gets easy to forget this. Even the authors have this problem (see the aforementioned How Do You Do That? for many, many, many examples). Nevertheless, Psychics don\u2019t add Mind just because they are using their mind. Shamans don\u2019t add Spirit to everything they do, just the stuff that Spirit actually covers. VAs don\u2019t add Forces just because their computers use electricity. Verbena don\u2019t have to add Life when they use blood as a focus. Etc.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Now to the second part of your question, what happens when the psychic uses a non-Mind spell and another mage scans for psychic energies? And really this is part of a bigger question, which is what happens when one character scans for something that is a paradigm element of another character?<br /> <br /> And this is indeed a very broad question and you are right that this could lead to lots of interesting scenes and exploration of paradigm, because paradigms frequently don\u2019t interact well and mages often make claims that other mages can\u2019t verify. In fact the existence of the sphere system in universe indicates it\u2019s been a problem for at least as long as the Traditions have been around.<br /> <br /> In general this isn\u2019t a problem because the principles of most mages practices are complex and not easily broken down into a single sphere. That\u2019s actually true in your example too. Despite the name, the nebulous idea \u2018psychic energy\u2019 is not obviously the province of Mind. To give just one example, the game Trinity bases psychic powers on subatomic particles called Psions, and though that game has nothing to do with Mage, there\u2019s nothing saying a mage couldn\u2019t have a similar view of the world.<br /> <br /> Or to bring it around to my first point. When Anne scans for the use of Mind, she is mostly scanning for influence and power exercised over minds and she\u2019s not going to find it because Terry isn\u2019t doing that. And since both she and Terry know that (hopefully Anne does anyways) neither of them will be surprised. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-13T09:06:15-07:00","id":1558835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>twig</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1558768-shperes-over-paradigm-or-not?p=1558817#post1558817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Essentially, to Terry, Forces comes from mental energy, whatever other Mages might say. And to be fair to him, if you were to turn off his brain, he wouldn't be able to use Forces! The mind does seem to be crucial.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, that's true for the vast majority of mages. Very few of them can cast as an unconscious heap on the floor, whether or not the Mind sphere is involved.<br /> <br /> But lets say that instead we are talking about some effect which interferes with the ability to focus or concentrate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sistofelis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1558768-shperes-over-paradigm-or-not?p=1558824#post1558824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a great point to help me further explain my doubt!<br /> <br /> Suppose Terry's brain has been shut down.<br /> <br /> IF we take away the possibility for him to use Force (since according to his paradigm, those comes from his Mind), then we're putting &quot;Paradigm&quot; over &quot;Spheres&quot; in terms of what is predominant in influencing the fiction (where &quot;Fiction&quot; as I intended is the &quot;narrative reality of the game&quot;).<br /> And that could be absolutely fine, but that would mean that Terry's paradigm would put Mind as a pre requisite to use the other spheres. Wich I'll admit can be intriguing from a rp stand point, but it's not (as far as I know) a rule.<br /> <br /> IF we would allow Terry to access forces even when his Mind is turned off, then we would be leaning more towards a Sphere (as in &quot;the dots the character has on his sheets) over Paradigm, in terms of what influence more, again, the fiction.<br /> <br /> That's the core of my doubt, thanks for providing me a hook to elaborate (I hope) better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Targeting the use of a specific sphere is not, to my knowledge, possible unless that sphere is connected to specific practices and foci the other ones are not. Take away a unique focus and you definitely mess with the mage. Terry seems to use his brain for at least Forces and presumably Mind, so I don't see how anyone could target just one of them.<br /> <br /> But for the larger question of how to handle events that mess with Terry's ability to use his brain (concussions, mental influence, etc.) I find this to be an excellent use of the Abilities Enhancing Magic rules. Use skill checks to represent particular practices and use difficulty modifiers to represent any relevant modifiers. Terry might reasonably use Meditation rolls for instance, with a concussion imposing a +1 or +2 difficulty.<br /> <br /> And of course if his brain is actually turned off, he can't make the roll at all. But again, few rolls can be made when the character is unconscious.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-14T09:20:02-07:00","id":1558853,"title":"","content":"Exception: Wild Talent is arguably the mage's Avatar casting on its own. It can happen whenever the Storyteller says that it does, and the state of the mage's mind has nothing to do with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-15T04:08:02-07:00","id":1558867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sistofelis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1558768-shperes-over-paradigm-or-not#post1558768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">snip<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Terry's paradigm is not being challenged. Since true magic in the World of Darkness series is fueled by the power of your belief in it, Terry is actually correct in that his powers stem from the strength of his mental focus.<br /> <br /> The difference with what Terry believes vs what his friend sees could be applied to quite literally any other paradigm.<br /> <br /> For example, the Celestial Choristers believe that all magic originates from The One. Yet you have people like the Verbena and the Akashics who are channeling myriad different gods and goddesses, or the Dreamspeakers who are making contact with nature spirits.<br /> <br /> <br /> Spheres dictate what kind of feats your magic is capable of performing, while Paradigms dictate HOW you are able to perform those feats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-15T12:45:11-07:00","id":1558875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1558768-shperes-over-paradigm-or-not?p=1558820#post1558820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreed, psychic powers it's not a great example because &quot;Warping reality with your mind&quot; and &quot;Warping reality with your Will&quot; are very similar concepts :P . It <i>could</i> be a problem if there's a power that blocks or detects psychic numina but wouldn't work on Magic(k) - but then one could question the reliability of said power. But, yeah, this is an issue for many Paradigms.<br /> <br /> Spirits that should be present, but you can clearly see they aren't (with Spirit 2) it's the classic example. Another example could be &quot;what happens if you sabbotage the machinery a Technocrat it's using as an Instrument - does still function if the Technocrat doesn't know it shouldn't?&quot;<br /> <br /> There's two ways AFAIK to rule this, that are both supported in the books to at least some extent.<br /> <br /> *One school of tought it's that magick will work as long as the mage believes it does. This can lead to situations where belief it's challenged (the Technocrat it's giving maintenance to his gizmo, and discovers the sabbotage, yet it worked a second ago)<br /> <br /> *Another it's that Paradigm works at a &quot;meta level&quot; and thus if it's &quot;technology&quot; and there's a reason &quot;technology&quot; shouldn't work, then it won't work (wheter the mage knows about it or not). This can be confusing and a bit difficult to adjudicate (when the books try, it often looks like a punishment: Like with the Spirit prerequisite for Shamanic practices on HDYDT), but I think it's the most thematic if it can be done well.<br /> <br /> The first option it's the canon answer of 1rst edition. Back then all mages knew on a level they were reality warping with their willpower, but needed instruments because of inexperience. Latter on Mages started to actually <i>believe </i>ontheir Paradigm, and thus the 2nd option surges as an interesting posibility, but the 1rst one was never really abandoned.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a>. I use the second option in my Mage games and it usually works out pretty well, but I know Storytellers who have used the first option (usually because they believe it\u2019s the most literally consistent with the old school Mage rules) and don\u2019t have any problems running things that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-16T03:03:16-07:00","id":1558881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1558768-shperes-over-paradigm-or-not?p=1558831#post1558831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I see, you're wondering about cases where the Paradigm posits as the &quot;cause&quot; of the effect an element that belongs under the conceptual umbrella of another Sphere that wasn't involved on the effect. So what now?<br /> <br /> Core RAW, no: What matters for the mechanics are the mechanics of the Effect, not the mechanics thta could be alluded by Paradigm. So, levitating it's Forces regardless of your belief.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I believe too, and I agree. Levitating is Force, and to your next point...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1558768-shperes-over-paradigm-or-not?p=1558831#post1558831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> HDYDT has a (very unpopular) optional rule where, yes, you should have the Sphere of the concept as prerequisite. Shamans need to have Spirit 2 and include it on every Effect. In the case of psychic powers, Mind 2, or maybe even 3, would be a prerequisite to cast your levitation effect. Ppl call this &quot;Sphere Tax&quot;<br /> <br /> There's something to be said in favor of HDYDT &quot;Sphere Tax&quot;, tho - it often isn't as onerous as it looks like because Paradigms that are deeply invested on the phenomena of some Sphere are most likely going to gravitate to that Sphere anyways (so it's a &quot;tax&quot; that you were going to pay anyway). And, mechanically, it adds the flavorful <i>dis</i>advantage that your spells associated with that Sphere can be sensed and/or countered by using the additional Sphere. I.E: If you use &quot;fire spirits&quot; for Forces, and thus have to add Spirit 2 to the mix, then you can counter the spell with Spirit.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm very familiar with &quot;Sphere Tax&quot;, and in fact, to get back to my original example, I believe HDYDT states that levitate could be achieved with mind. I don't have the books with me, and i can't recall if its stated as a prerequisite (as per &quot;Sphere Tax&quot;), or outright a substitute. Either way, it muds the water.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1558768-shperes-over-paradigm-or-not?p=1558831#post1558831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem with that optional rule it's that it's all disadvantages, it's flavorful but it sort of fells like a punishment - even if not a very severe one.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'll admit I like a certain degree in polishing when it comes to spell.<br /> So yeah, if a player throws in additional spheres to refine, or round up a magical effect, I'm all for it.<br /> But that should never goes in the direction of the &quot;Sphere Tax&quot; or unnecessary or stretched requirements.<br /> Then again, often &quot;less is more&quot;, working the opposite way, not additive but subtractive can lead to simpl\u00f2ier and equally beautiful conception of magical effects.<br /> But that's maybe out of topic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1558768-shperes-over-paradigm-or-not?p=1558831#post1558831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I preffer to detach Spheres and Paradigms at the level of mechanics, and if anything rejoin them on the level of the narrative afterwards. To me, Forces when used by a psychic <i>it's</i> psychic. It doesn't <i>need</i> Mind to be psychic. It needs Mind if he wants to add stuff like telepathy to his arsenal of psychic powers.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think this summarize my approach as well. I was afraid I was missing the point, but this whole thread has helped me in find a better footing!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28492-sistofelis","name":"Sistofelis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-16T03:31:59-07:00","id":1558883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1558768-shperes-over-paradigm-or-not?p=1558834#post1558834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In neither case do the Spheres cover anything to do with how a mage paradigmatically gets to the effect, and usually this is really clear. However, whenever a paradigm starts to sound a lot like a specific sphere (commonly Mind, Spirit, and Prime) it gets easy to forget this. Even the authors have this problem (see the aforementioned How Do You Do That? for many, many, many examples). Nevertheless, Psychics don\u2019t add Mind just because they are using their mind. Shamans don\u2019t add Spirit to everything they do, just the stuff that Spirit actually covers. VAs don\u2019t add Forces just because their computers use electricity. Verbena don\u2019t have to add Life when they use blood as a focus. Etc.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I agrre, Mind,Spirit, and prime are the trickiest one.<br /> What are you explaining is exactly my point of view, where I stumbled was, as you point out, the second part of my question...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1558768-shperes-over-paradigm-or-not?p=1558834#post1558834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now to the second part of your question, what happens when the psychic uses a non-Mind spell and another mage scans for psychic energies? And really this is part of a bigger question, which is what happens when one character scans for something that is a paradigm element of another character?<br /> <br /> And this is indeed a very broad question and you are right that this could lead to lots of interesting scenes and exploration of paradigm, because paradigms frequently don\u2019t interact well and mages often make claims that other mages can\u2019t verify. In fact the existence of the sphere system in universe indicates it\u2019s been a problem for at least as long as the Traditions have been around.<br /> <br /> (...)<br /> <br /> Or to bring it around to my first point. When Anne scans for the use of Mind, she is mostly scanning for influence and power exercised over minds and she\u2019s not going to find it because Terry isn\u2019t doing that. And since both she and Terry know that (hopefully Anne does anyways) neither of them will be surprised.</div> </div> </div> </div>You nailed the core of my doubt. And I think all I needed was some sort of corroboration that my approach was... I wouldn't say correct, but at least shared amongst others.<br /> What you point out is indeed, a simple yet, effective solution. <br /> <br /> &quot;Let them discuss and see what happens!&quot;<br /> Wich is an important part (at least for me) in how character develope, and yes, how they can deepen their understanding of &quot;what is Magick&quot; (either by broadening, deepening or...doing both in regard to their paradigm).<br /> <br /> But sometimes it's just like that. This game offers so many hints (and admittedly lack to explain a lot) that it's easy to fall into some rabbit holes. But then again, I think it's a major part of its charm.<br /> Sometimes trying to figure out the different facet and approcaches of the game itself, feels not unlike what the characters of our stories do, trying to figure out Mafgic itself.<br /> <br /> I'm glad I came here to put my doubts on the table because everyone who contribute in this thread helped me a lot to see it through.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28492-sistofelis","name":"Sistofelis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-30T14:09:02-07:00","id":1559124,"title":"","content":"The other thing to keep in mind is that Terry's paradigm is not the problem in the example given, Anne's is. Anne is presumably using Mind in her scan and deciding that covers all psychic activity.<br /> consider if Marget enters after Anne, hears the conversation and retorts, &quot;Anne, you are using the lowest setting on the psychcorder. Read the manual. There are nine known spectrums of psychic activity. You are only scanning for one. Check your settings. Also how many spectrums are you trained for?&quot;<br /> I play this the same for Spirit. Spirit 2 can allow a mage to talk directly with a spirit and maybe ask a favor. Forces or any other Sphere means that the mage does not need to talk to the anthropomorphic manifestation of a spirit; they know how to encourage the spirit to act as needed. Spirits are fickle, but they are also predictable and when stimulated properly will follow their nature.<br /> so let's say Anthony, who is in good with spirits, uses Forces 2 to pull circles of flame from a lit candle and Anne walks in, uses Spirit 1 to scan for spirits and, nit detecting any use if spirit magic, tries to denounce Anthony as a fraud. Margaret follows and chastises her again.<br /> &quot;You are looking for the spirit carrying the fire. Something from across the Gauntlet. You need to look to the spirit the fire is carrying, right in front of you.&quot; (You need to use Forces to see the spirits Anthony is influencing. Spirits are in all things, so any Sphere magic will involve a spirit). This may seem semantics, because it is, but with magic, semantics form paradigm and paradigm shapes reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12269-heilong","user":"Heilong","date":". 03-30-2026, 05:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12269-heilong","name":"Heilong","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-31T21:53:16-07:00","id":1559157,"title":"","content":"On a side note, am I correct in the understanding that the Technocracy views Sorcery as an expression of psychic powers?<br /> <br /> Because if so, that could be a potential story hook for trying to recruit him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-01T14:02:14-07:00","id":1559169,"title":"","content":"That is one aspect but not the full view. Any scientist, archeologist, political thinker, or auto mechanic who works above peak performance is likely an Extraordinary Citizen leveraging the Technocratic paradigm and systems, whether they know anything about the Technocracy or not.<br /> Psychics and psychic abilities in humans are simply an area of interest for the Technocracy, particularly the NWO.<br /> All hens are chickens, but not all chickens are psychic.<br /> but yes, there are some that are really serious that psychic abilities shows peak human evolution and are happy to run Sleepers by the hundreds or thousands through experimental programs and either processing the failures by dumping the damaged people to wander the streets or dumping the bodies in undisclosed locations.<br /> story could be as dark or campy as you like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12269-heilong","name":"Heilong","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-01T14:58:04-07:00","id":1559170,"title":"","content":"Another way to put it might be by way of analogy with Awakened Mages and Technocrats.<br /> <br /> From the Technocrat perspective, Sorcerers could be seen as using Psychic Powers in the same way Mages are (mis)using the principles of Enlightened Science when they perform &quot;Magic.&quot; Their methods are inferior, if not actively dangerous, because they are guided by ignorant superstition rather than a rational understanding of 'natural' laws.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-10T05:03:18-07:00","id":1559325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>twig</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1558768-shperes-over-paradigm-or-not?p=1558817#post1558817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The trickier example is Mages who believe all their powers come from spirits or aliens or other unearthly forces. How does that Mage explain it when their powers work, only to then be told that they are 100% cut off from the Umbra and there's no way any spirit could have manifested the effect? Presumably they'd just cope and say that these forces can pierce reality via their Avatar, but still, it's interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some suggestions: <br /> <br /> 1. They don't think of the entity as a spirit. A deity to them is not a spirit. <br /> 1.b They do think of it as a spirit but far more powerful than normal and able to circumvent things.<br /> <br /> 2. You can shortcut to the astral plane through your dreams, you don't have to go trough the penumbra or so on to get there. So either parts of that path is still open or there's some other hidden path.<br /> <br /> 3. The spirit resides in the normal world, so you don't have to reach the umbra to commune with it. Example: there's a tree let's talk to it.<br /> <br /> 4. The gifts of their chosen patron were granted them a long time ago, such as when they awakened. They don't rely on him to fuel up on powers they just need to live according to the correct strictures to use the blessings they have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28924-tjalei","name":"Tjalei","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-18T04:48:22-07:00","id":1561887,"title":"","content":"I think there's an important aspect, or interpretation, of what a Paradigm is, missing here.<br /> <br /> A Mage's belief shapes reality.<br /> <br /> But not necessarily on a mere perceptual level: on an ontological level.<br /> <br /> What they believe is reality for them, and their awareness of the situation doesn't change that.<br /> <br /> Let me give 3 examples:<br /> <br /> 1. Our psychic guy, Terry, is levitating with Forces 2. We can even say he doesn't <i><b>have</b></i> Mind.<br /> <br /> First, one thing to be clear about<b></b>: if Anne is looking if he uses Mind, she's doing it wrong. Not because of Paradigm at all, but because she's looking for a Mind <i><b>effect</b></i>, not a mental state.<br /> <br /> But what if she looks for the <i><b>mental state</b></i> of a psychic?<br /> <br /> <u><b>IT WORKS</b></u><br /> <br /> He IS a psychic. His Paradigm can't give him direct control over the &quot;psychic mental state&quot; because it's a Mind effect, but he is a psychic because his Paradigm made him a Psychic long ago, even if a psychic that uses Spheres rather than Numina. He achieves the state the same way any psychic does, and if an observer can detect this, it is detected.<br /> <br /> 2. A shaman girl has no Spirit sphere or just didn't use it. She does know what they are, and she does know a spirit must be present for her powers to work.<br /> <br /> Unknown to her, there's no spirits in the area, whatever the cause. She tries her contact ritual to increase a flame with Forces. What happens is that...<br /> <br /> It doesn't work. Her powers don't work without spirits. She knows that, and that's ontologically true. <b>It's not a belief, <i>it's a fact</i></b>, even if it's her belief what made it into a fact.<br /> <br /> That's the power of Magic, for good and ill.<br /> <br /> 3. Same goes for secretly broken or sabotaged Technocratic Instrument.<br /> <br /> In fact, that's a relatively common thing in the Union. They have plenty of inner conflicts and conspiracies, and you know what they do? They <i>sabotage Devices <u>and Instruments</u></i> if they can.<br /> <br /> The most ludicrous machines can work in their hands. But they must be what they expect to be. If the theory accepts that cardboard works as a gun barrel if it has aluminum coating, it does, but if the coat is actually silver paint with no aluminum, or the coat was removed without them noticing, it won't work. It's not the correct Instrument, and that's the end of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}